<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n97148" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρᾰτόπεδ-ον</span></b> , τό,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>camp, encampment</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				5.63
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				79
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				10
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				15.709
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Στρατόπεδα</span>, name of a
			part of Egypt, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.154
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				112
			</span></i>: hence, <i>encamped army</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				4.114
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				15.119
			</span></i>, etc.; in both senses, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.81
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> at Rome, the
				<i>Castra Praetoriana</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				60.1
			</span></i>, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			generally, <i>army</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.77
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				9.51
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				53
			</span></i>; also, <i>squadron</i> of ships, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				8.94
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.117
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				21.6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12.105.29
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. ναυτικὰ καὶ πεζικά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>HG</u>
					6.3.18
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> the Roman
				<i>legion</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				1.16.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>BGU</u>
				362 xi 15
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii A.D.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				55.23
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>the court</i> or <i>suite</i> of the emperor or his
			representative, <i><span class="en">
				Jul.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				46
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
